1
00:00:05,068 --> 00:00:06,736
It's finally here.

2
00:00:06,820 --> 00:00:08,947
Midori's first love.

3
00:00:09,030 --> 00:00:09,906
Could it be…

4
00:00:10,532 --> 00:00:13,409
you have come to dislike us?

5
00:00:13,493 --> 00:00:17,080
But Midori is completely
unused to romance.

6
00:00:17,580 --> 00:00:18,414
I…

7
00:00:18,498 --> 00:00:20,125
Mr. Nishigami…

8
00:00:20,208 --> 00:00:21,960
A typhoon is coming soon.

9
00:00:22,043 --> 00:00:25,421
Those five you are
so close with will all die.

10
00:00:25,505 --> 00:00:29,092
Your recent actions
have been unacceptable.

11
00:00:29,175 --> 00:00:32,095
You haven't forgotten
your mission, have you?

12
00:00:32,178 --> 00:00:35,682
You taught us many things and helped us.

13
00:00:36,266 --> 00:00:39,269
So we've had a fun and safe vacation.

14
00:00:39,352 --> 00:00:40,478
Three.

15
00:00:40,562 --> 00:00:41,396
Two.

16
00:00:41,479 --> 00:00:42,313
One.

17
00:00:43,398 --> 00:00:45,817
Thank you for always protecting the villa.

18
00:00:53,116 --> 00:00:57,078
Typhoon No.13 is expected
to maintain its extreme intensity,

19
00:00:57,162 --> 00:01:00,456
and make landfall
in the Kanto region late tonight.

20
00:01:00,540 --> 00:01:02,208
The typhoon scares me!

21
00:01:02,292 --> 00:01:05,086
This typhoon is quite strong, huh.

22
00:01:05,170 --> 00:01:07,547
It will probably miss us.
It's always like that.

23
00:01:07,630 --> 00:01:09,632
The news is just trying to scare us.

24
00:01:09,716 --> 00:01:10,675
That's true.

25
00:01:10,758 --> 00:01:14,345
You think work might be canceled tomorrow,
but then you wake up, and it's sunny.

26
00:01:14,429 --> 00:01:17,098
Looks like it will rain
quite a bit this time.

27
00:01:17,182 --> 00:01:19,434
I don't think I can fish in this weather.

28
00:01:20,185 --> 00:01:22,187
Then, what can we do indoors?

29
00:01:23,104 --> 00:01:24,022
Okay!

30
00:01:24,105 --> 00:01:26,357
Tonight, let's hold one of these!

31
00:01:26,441 --> 00:01:28,109
-Huh?
-What?

32
00:01:28,192 --> 00:01:30,194
-What is "these"?
-Here goes.

33
00:01:32,322 --> 00:01:33,656
What is it?

34
00:01:35,408 --> 00:01:36,910
Shut up!

35
00:01:38,411 --> 00:01:40,955
-We will hold a card tournament!
-Huh?

36
00:01:41,039 --> 00:01:42,457
In this day and age?

37
00:01:42,540 --> 00:01:44,626
Why not? I found these cards here.

38
00:01:44,709 --> 00:01:46,711
-I wonder if Grandma used them?
-They're big.

39
00:01:46,794 --> 00:01:49,339
-They are, right?
-What game should we play?

40
00:01:49,422 --> 00:01:50,798
-They're huge!
-Old Maid!

41
00:01:50,882 --> 00:01:53,009
-Old Maid using Grandma's cards!
-So big!

42
00:01:53,092 --> 00:01:55,220
-The heck is that?
-Stop it!

43
00:01:55,303 --> 00:01:56,346
This is the Old Maid card.

44
00:01:56,429 --> 00:01:58,264
I drew an old maid!

45
00:01:58,348 --> 00:02:00,016
Grandma, I'm sorry!

46
00:02:00,099 --> 00:02:00,975
Here.

47
00:02:01,059 --> 00:02:02,352
-You don't have it?
-Pick whichever.

48
00:02:02,435 --> 00:02:04,938
-You don't have it, right? Okay.
-Nope, I don't.

49
00:02:05,021 --> 00:02:07,941
Okay! Huh, what is this? Can I pick?

50
00:02:08,024 --> 00:02:10,109
-Will Mr. Nishigami come?
-Oh, sorry!

51
00:02:11,611 --> 00:02:14,364
He may be busy preparing for the typhoon.

52
00:02:14,447 --> 00:02:15,281
Right.

53
00:03:15,508 --> 00:03:17,719
Looks like a fun time, huh?

54
00:03:17,802 --> 00:03:18,845
A barbecue?

55
00:03:18,928 --> 00:03:20,138
JAPAN DIVISION HEAD
LADY YOMI

56
00:03:20,221 --> 00:03:21,514
Nice to be young.

57
00:03:23,516 --> 00:03:25,768
Sorry for calling you here so suddenly.

58
00:03:26,936 --> 00:03:27,812
Now…

59
00:03:30,440 --> 00:03:32,108
This is your final warning.

60
00:03:33,609 --> 00:03:35,945
Tonight is the night.

61
00:03:37,405 --> 00:03:41,117
Let me tell you what will happen
if you break the code.

62
00:03:42,744 --> 00:03:44,912
Every human involved with you

63
00:03:44,996 --> 00:03:48,458
will have all Grim Reaper
related memories erased.

64
00:03:48,541 --> 00:03:52,045
In other words,
they will forget your very existence.

65
00:03:53,004 --> 00:03:56,341
Every memory you shared this summer.

66
00:03:58,176 --> 00:04:02,513
The feelings that girl has for you
will also disappear.

67
00:04:03,765 --> 00:04:04,891
And of course,

68
00:04:05,433 --> 00:04:10,021
you yourself will be punished
by the laws of the underworld.

69
00:04:13,066 --> 00:04:14,525
Calm down.

70
00:04:15,109 --> 00:04:17,653
It's just a difference of a few decades.

71
00:04:18,613 --> 00:04:22,950
Those humans will just meet
their demise a bit earlier.

72
00:04:24,285 --> 00:04:26,579
Do your job, as you have always done.

73
00:04:27,538 --> 00:04:28,748
Don't forget.

74
00:04:29,499 --> 00:04:31,125
You're a Grim Reaper.

75
00:04:32,877 --> 00:04:37,590
Time flows differently
for us and for humans.

76
00:04:41,427 --> 00:04:43,054
I understand.

77
00:05:24,429 --> 00:05:25,847
No lying!

78
00:05:25,930 --> 00:05:27,598
It's a real weak one!

79
00:05:27,682 --> 00:05:29,016
A weak one.

80
00:05:29,100 --> 00:05:30,268
How about mine?

81
00:05:37,441 --> 00:05:39,152
I wonder what it's supposed to be?

82
00:05:39,986 --> 00:05:43,406
Did you copy it from a manga
you liked back in grade school?

83
00:05:43,489 --> 00:05:44,824
Hmm…

84
00:05:45,366 --> 00:05:47,285
Doesn't this look like Mr. Nishigami?

85
00:05:47,869 --> 00:05:48,786
Oh, really?

86
00:05:48,870 --> 00:05:49,787
Yeah.

87
00:05:51,330 --> 00:05:56,544
So he's been your dream guy
ever since you were a kid?

88
00:05:56,627 --> 00:05:58,462
-Right?
-I wonder.

89
00:06:00,381 --> 00:06:02,216
Is Mr. Nishigami not coming?

90
00:06:02,300 --> 00:06:03,134
Yeah…

91
00:06:03,217 --> 00:06:05,887
On a day like this,
shouldn't he come to check on us?

92
00:06:05,970 --> 00:06:09,432
I guess he's busy with the typhoon,
since he's the caretaker here.

93
00:06:11,809 --> 00:06:13,186
Oh, it's him!

94
00:06:13,269 --> 00:06:14,437
What? Mr. Nishigami?

95
00:06:20,026 --> 00:06:21,068
Mr. Nishigami.

96
00:06:40,796 --> 00:06:42,965
Mr. Nishigami, please sit in the middle.

97
00:06:43,049 --> 00:06:44,717
-Six cans!
-Okay!

98
00:06:44,800 --> 00:06:46,552
Konta, another round of Old Maid?

99
00:06:46,636 --> 00:06:48,304
I'm tired of Old Maid already!

100
00:06:48,387 --> 00:06:49,222
It's fine.

101
00:06:49,305 --> 00:06:51,015
-Isn't there anything else?
-What?

102
00:06:51,098 --> 00:06:53,392
I bet you haven't played cards
in a while either.

103
00:06:53,476 --> 00:06:55,269
How long since your last game?

104
00:06:55,353 --> 00:06:57,188
Still, I wonder if we'll be okay.

105
00:06:57,271 --> 00:06:59,357
Is it always like this around here?

106
00:06:59,440 --> 00:07:03,611
No, this typhoon
is an especially large one.

107
00:07:03,694 --> 00:07:05,947
I'm sure it will be fine.

108
00:07:06,030 --> 00:07:08,074
It's not raining that much yet.

109
00:07:09,659 --> 00:07:12,453
Will you have dinner with us today too?

110
00:07:12,537 --> 00:07:15,998
But, Midori, do we still have food?
I don't think we can buy anything now.

111
00:07:16,082 --> 00:07:18,668
True, feels like it will start raining
the moment we step outside.

112
00:07:18,751 --> 00:07:22,255
Yeah. So today, with leftovers,
I'll make Napolitan pasta.

113
00:07:22,338 --> 00:07:23,506
Oh, Napolitan!

114
00:07:23,589 --> 00:07:26,259
We can't do a barbecue,
but I'll make a yummy napolitan.

115
00:07:26,342 --> 00:07:27,176
Sure.

116
00:07:27,260 --> 00:07:29,428
Mr. Nishigami,
you should just call it a day.

117
00:07:29,512 --> 00:07:31,013
Yeah, that's right.

118
00:07:31,514 --> 00:07:32,557
Let's drink.

119
00:07:32,640 --> 00:07:35,059
-Here you go.
-Yeah!

120
00:07:35,810 --> 00:07:37,144
Thank you.

121
00:07:37,228 --> 00:07:38,312
What are we playing?

122
00:07:38,396 --> 00:07:39,272
-Daifugo!
-Daifugo!

123
00:07:51,909 --> 00:07:52,827
What?

124
00:08:00,293 --> 00:08:01,752
Mr. Nishigami?

125
00:08:10,344 --> 00:08:11,178
What?

126
00:08:12,054 --> 00:08:13,514
Such a thing is impossible!

127
00:08:14,181 --> 00:08:15,099
I mean,

128
00:08:15,182 --> 00:08:20,646
the typhoon passes through multiple areas,
so I can't just divert it by myself.

129
00:08:20,730 --> 00:08:21,606
It's beyond me.

130
00:08:22,231 --> 00:08:25,026
Besides, such an urgent request?

131
00:08:25,109 --> 00:08:27,278
A god on my level can't do it.

132
00:08:31,032 --> 00:08:33,409
Don't look so scary! I can't do it!

133
00:08:33,492 --> 00:08:37,413
You know if we try anything,
we will be punished, right?

134
00:08:37,496 --> 00:08:40,333
Besides, what you want to stop
is the landslide, right?

135
00:08:40,416 --> 00:08:43,210
So, why not ask the Mountain God?

136
00:08:43,294 --> 00:08:45,755
The Mountain God. Go ask them, yeah.

137
00:08:45,838 --> 00:08:48,758
No one can stop that typhoon,
but the Mountain God…

138
00:08:49,300 --> 00:08:51,260
The ground is within her control.

139
00:08:51,344 --> 00:08:53,971
If you ask them,
they can do something. Okay?

140
00:08:54,055 --> 00:08:54,972
Oh, he's gone.

141
00:08:55,056 --> 00:08:56,932
Where did he go? Huh?

142
00:09:00,561 --> 00:09:03,564
At this rate,
he will be punished, for sure.

143
00:09:08,402 --> 00:09:09,862
What are you saying?

144
00:09:10,363 --> 00:09:12,198
You're a Grim Reaper, aren't you?

145
00:09:13,866 --> 00:09:17,536
Please stop the landslide
that is about to happen.

146
00:09:19,163 --> 00:09:20,831
What are you saying?

147
00:09:21,457 --> 00:09:24,418
Lady Yomi already warned you many times.

148
00:09:25,252 --> 00:09:28,714
Don't interfere
with the destiny of humans.

149
00:09:30,132 --> 00:09:32,677
-Yes.
-Listen up, Reaper.

150
00:09:33,219 --> 00:09:35,638
Even if you violate
the laws of the underworld

151
00:09:35,721 --> 00:09:40,017
and give up your existence to save them,

152
00:09:40,810 --> 00:09:43,104
they'll die in a few decades anyway.

153
00:09:44,188 --> 00:09:45,439
A few decades.

154
00:09:45,523 --> 00:09:46,607
No.

155
00:09:46,691 --> 00:09:49,360
Some of them might only have a few years.

156
00:09:50,486 --> 00:09:52,029
For this past month,

157
00:09:53,114 --> 00:09:56,867
I've been watching those humans
spending time at that villa.

158
00:09:57,868 --> 00:10:00,538
They don't work, they don't study.

159
00:10:01,080 --> 00:10:04,375
They just idle away every day
playing around.

160
00:10:05,042 --> 00:10:07,753
Even if you save them tonight,

161
00:10:08,629 --> 00:10:15,136
their self-indulgent and meaningless life
will only be extended by a little bit.

162
00:10:16,721 --> 00:10:18,264
I believe

163
00:10:18,347 --> 00:10:24,603
that the time they spent at this villa
will pave the way for their future.

164
00:10:24,687 --> 00:10:29,024
Besides, to them, it's a long time.

165
00:10:29,108 --> 00:10:32,445
A few decades to them should be equivalent

166
00:10:33,404 --> 00:10:34,780
to hundreds…

167
00:10:35,448 --> 00:10:36,449
No.

168
00:10:37,450 --> 00:10:40,911
Thousands of years for us.

169
00:10:46,292 --> 00:10:49,462
You talk just like a human now!

170
00:10:50,129 --> 00:10:51,213
You…

171
00:10:53,382 --> 00:10:56,302
You'll be erased like sand
by Lady Yomi, you know.

172
00:10:57,470 --> 00:10:58,888
Like sand…

173
00:11:04,393 --> 00:11:07,813
A Reaper like me will die…

174
00:11:12,818 --> 00:11:13,986
It's strange.

175
00:11:14,570 --> 00:11:17,281
Right now, for the first time,

176
00:11:19,950 --> 00:11:21,118
I truly feel

177
00:11:21,744 --> 00:11:24,413
like I'm alive.

178
00:11:33,547 --> 00:11:34,590
Seriously!

179
00:11:35,966 --> 00:11:38,928
A Grim Reaper, taken in by humans…

180
00:11:39,470 --> 00:11:41,222
That's a first for me.

181
00:11:46,685 --> 00:11:47,978
I, too,

182
00:11:49,396 --> 00:11:54,193
have been watching the humans
living in Tatsumi Town for a long time.

183
00:11:55,903 --> 00:11:59,823
And while there are humans who fulfill
their lifespan, less than 100 years,

184
00:11:59,907 --> 00:12:02,910
and meet death peacefully,

185
00:12:03,953 --> 00:12:08,541
there are also those
who die young due to illness or accidents.

186
00:12:11,835 --> 00:12:12,836
You…

187
00:12:13,796 --> 00:12:17,091
want to extend the time
of those young people, don't you?

188
00:12:18,342 --> 00:12:22,388
Even if you must offer
your own existence in exchange.

189
00:12:26,225 --> 00:12:28,727
A Grim Reaper, breaking the code.

190
00:12:31,522 --> 00:12:32,815
How interesting.

191
00:12:36,610 --> 00:12:38,112
Up on that mountain,

192
00:12:39,196 --> 00:12:41,615
there is an old shrine nobody visits.

193
00:12:42,575 --> 00:12:44,034
Try going there.

194
00:12:45,452 --> 00:12:50,666
All natural disasters around here
are governed by that shrine.

195
00:12:51,959 --> 00:12:55,212
If you go there, you may be able…

196
00:12:56,380 --> 00:12:58,507
to change something.

197
00:12:59,925 --> 00:13:01,093
Not that I care.

198
00:13:01,927 --> 00:13:06,015
Over here, the rain and wind from earlier
have temporarily stopped.

199
00:13:06,098 --> 00:13:08,976
Could this be the calm before the storm?

200
00:13:09,059 --> 00:13:11,645
However, the intensity of the typhoon
has not dropped.

201
00:13:11,729 --> 00:13:14,064
Please do not let your guard down.

202
00:13:20,279 --> 00:13:23,490
Where did he go?

203
00:14:17,211 --> 00:14:19,838
A Grim Reaper in human form?

204
00:14:19,922 --> 00:14:21,757
A Grim Reaper…

205
00:14:21,840 --> 00:14:23,300
Are you here to collect me?

206
00:14:27,304 --> 00:14:28,555
I'm sorry.

207
00:14:28,639 --> 00:14:30,683
I can't die. Yeah.

208
00:14:31,350 --> 00:14:34,019
Because I'm a god.

209
00:15:10,973 --> 00:15:13,559
Japan is home to myriad gods.

210
00:15:13,642 --> 00:15:16,311
I control all weather!

211
00:15:16,395 --> 00:15:19,314
The venerable Dragon God!

212
00:15:19,398 --> 00:15:22,484
Today, without a doubt,
a landslide will occur.

213
00:15:22,568 --> 00:15:25,070
You cannot change that absolute fact.

214
00:15:25,154 --> 00:15:26,405
Goodbye.

215
00:15:26,488 --> 00:15:29,033
They're being blown away!

216
00:15:29,658 --> 00:15:31,410
It's dangerous to stay here.

217
00:15:34,413 --> 00:15:35,497
Mr. Nishigami?

218
00:15:35,581 --> 00:15:38,250
I have met you before.

219
00:15:39,710 --> 00:15:41,045
Who are you?

220
00:15:41,754 --> 00:15:43,255
It was the best vacation.

221
00:15:44,089 --> 00:15:45,090
Thank you.

222
00:15:46,050 --> 00:15:47,009
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.

